                  <msItem>
                     <title>Missale Sarisb.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The form of the ex libris of Ushaw College,
                        XVIII.F.4.18, written in Marian times, suggests that this missal was at St
                        John's College earlier in the sixteenth century and had been restored
                        there.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <physDesc> <typeDesc><p>Printed book.</p></typeDesc> </physDesc><history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate>Paris, A.D. 1503</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_107">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. St John's College</orgName><p>'Orate pro illius salute qui
                        hunc librum reseruauit et collegio diui Ioannis evangeliste proprio domino
                        restituit et ne sitis immemores primi donatoris sed pro anima eius ad deum
                        fundite preces vel in resurrectionis gloria inter sanctos et electos dei
                        resuscitat respirat' (s. xvi med.).</p><p>At end: oracio, secretum and
                        postcommunio for St Etheldreda, in MS.</p><p>These two inscriptions suggest
                        that this book belonged to St John's College, Cambridge, before the
                        Reformation and was restored in Marian times.</p></provenance>
               </history>
            </msDesc>
